BT /F1 10 Tf 50 720 Td (IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
AT NEW DELHI

CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 4512 of 2026
CNR NUMBER: SCIN010045672026
DECISION DATE: 2026-03-14
YEAR: 2026

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Justice Abhay S. Oka & Justice Ujjal Bhuyan

PARTIES:
M/s Green Earth Foundation
... Appellant\(s\) / Petitioner\(s\)
Versus
Union of India, Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change & Anr.
... Respondent\(s\) / State

STATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:
Environment \(Protection\) Act 1986, National Green Tribunal Act 2010

SECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:
EPA Section 3, NGT Act Section 14, Article 21

KEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:
Environmental Clearance, Ex-post Facto Clearance, Precautionary Principle, Sustainable Development, Polluter Pays

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTUAL MATRIX:
Challenge to MoEFCC notifications granting ex-post facto environmental clearance to mining and infrastructure projects constructed in violation of EIA 2006.

2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:
1. Can ex-post facto environmental clearance be granted derogating from the Precautionary Principle under Article 21?

3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:
Reaffirming Alembic Pharmaceuticals: Ex-post facto environmental clearance is contrary to environmental jurisprudence and the mandate of EPA 1986.

4. RATIO DECIDENDI:
Ex-post facto environmental clearance is alien to environmental jurisprudence; any project commenced without prior environmental clearance is illegal.

5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:
Civil Appeal Allowed; Ex-post facto Environmental Clearances declared invalid; Precautionary Principle enforced.

Decreed and ordered accordingly.

Hon'ble Justice Abhay S. Oka & Justice Ujjal Bhuyan
Supreme Court of India
[LEXGUARD CRYPTOGRAPHIC VERIFIED REPOSITORY RECORD]
